# Editor UI component catalog

Any change that **adds, removes, or changes the purpose or typical use** of a reusable Editor UI component **must** update [`docs/architecture/components.md`](../../docs/architecture/components.md) in the **same branch/PR**. Do not defer the catalog to a follow-up.

## What counts as reusable

| Layer | Path | Catalog section |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primitives | `packages/ui/src/components/` | `@babylonslate/ui` |
| Composites | `packages/editor-kit/src/` (exported React components) | `@babylonslate/editor-kit` |
| Graph shell | `packages/graph-ui/src/` (`GraphEditor`, `NodePalette`, and peers meant for reuse) | `@babylonslate/graph-ui` |
| App wrappers | `apps/editor/src/components/` used from **more than one** screen/panel | App wrappers |

Do **not** catalog one-off screens (Homepage, Play overlay, Settings modals, dock panels) or test-only files.

## How to update the catalog

- **New component** → add a row: name, one-line what it does, where it is used. List composition parts (`DialogTitle`, `FieldLabel`) on the family row, not as separate entries.
- **Changed behavior or call sites** → rewrite the definition / “Used for” so they stay true.
- **Removed or no longer reused** → delete the row (or move a single-call-site wrapper to the “Not kit” note).
- **New primitive or editor-kit composite** → also add it to the Component Gallery (`/?test=1&gallery=1`) when it is kit-level.
- Hooks and helpers (`useContextMenu`, `humanizePropertyLabel`) stay in the short “Related hooks” line, not the component table.

Keep rows short. Style: [docs.mdc](docs.mdc).
